    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d157">

                <pb facs="0301" n="209" xml:id="pg209"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Hay to Mr. Wu</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1899-02-06"><hi rendition="#italic">February 6,
                        1899</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 86.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge the receipt
                    of your note of February 3, in which you ask, for the information of your
                    Government, what policy the United States Government intends or is likely to
                    adopt in dealing with the question of Chinese immigration to the Philippine
                    islands, particularly during the period of military occupancy of those
                    territories.</p>
                <p>The subject is having the most careful consideration of this Government, but
                    until the military occupancy of the United States, now confined to certain
                    limited areas, is extended, and until fuller consideration can be given to the
                    matter in the light of the inquiry to be forth-with set on foot by the
                    Philippines Commission, which has been appointed to investigate the condition of
                    the islands, I shall be unable to make definite response to your inquiry.</p>
                <p>I shall send a copy of your note to the presiding officer of the Philippines
                    Commission for his information.</p>
                <p>Accept, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">John Hay</hi>.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
